    "created_at": "2024-06-25T14:00:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-06-25T14:00:16Z",
    "body": "The biggest thing we need to decide at the HTML level is, for each API which accepts callbacks, which AsyncContext.Snapshot should it be run in. Many of us are leaning towards \"the snapshot where the callback-accepting API was first called\".\r\n\r\nSome Web APIs could benefit from passing an additional AsyncContext.Shapshot instance to the callback, e.g., it might be useful for `window.onerror` to have access to the current snapshot when the exception was thrown--this could be an attribute attached to the Event, or the Error/DOMException, for example.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
